---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "June 2026";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms - Tempo"
  description="Terms of use for Tempo: free to use, no warranty, you're responsible for the actions you trigger and the scores you install or author.">
  <main class="legal">
    <h1>Terms of Service &amp; License</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p class="lede">
      Tempo v1.x is provided free of charge. You can use it for personal or
      commercial purposes. It comes with no warranty. You are responsible
      for the actions you trigger through it and for the scores you author,
      install, modify, or keep enabled.
    </p>

    <h2>License grant</h2>
    <p>
      You are granted a non-exclusive, non-transferable license to install and
      use Tempo on Macs you control, for any lawful purpose, at no cost. You
      may not redistribute, modify, reverse-engineer, or resell the Tempo
      application binary except as permitted by applicable law. You may freely
      write and share scores, configurations, and scripts that work with
      Tempo.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      Tempo is provided <strong>"as is"</strong>, without warranty of any
      kind, express or implied, including but not limited to the warranties of
      merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement.
      The author makes no guarantees that Tempo will be uninterrupted,
      error-free, or fit for your specific use case.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the author shall not
      be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or
      punitive damages, or any loss of data, revenue, profits, or business
      arising out of or in connection with your use of Tempo, even if advised
      of the possibility of such damages. Use Tempo at your own risk.
    </p>

    <h2>Scores and actions: you decide what runs</h2>
    <p>
      Tempo executes actions you trigger through "scores", small JSON files
      that declare the buttons attached to each event source. Tempo ships
      with a curated set of bundled scores installed and enabled by default
      so the application works on first launch; you can disable, modify, or
      remove any of them from Settings, and you can author your own or
      install additional ones from the public catalog.
    </p>
    <p>
      In v1.x every action runs only when you click its button. Tempo does
      not fire any action on your behalf: a score declares what a button
      does, but Tempo never executes it autonomously. A fresh installation
      contains no auto-firing automation, and v1.x will never introduce one.
    </p>
    <p>
      You are solely responsible for the actions you trigger and for the
      scores you author, install, modify, or keep enabled, including but
      not limited to: opening URLs, running Terminal commands, invoking
      AppleScripts, posting to third-party services, modifying system
      state, or interacting with HomeKit accessories. Tempo maintains a
      local audit log of every action you trigger so you can review what
      ran and when.
    </p>
    <p>
      Community-contributed scores, whether downloaded from the public Tempo
      Scores catalog or dropped into your local Scores folder from any other
      source, carry the same responsibility. The reviewed catalog includes a
      security and sanity check by the Tempo team, but that review is not a
      warranty. <strong>The functional responsibility of a score lies with
      its author, and the decision to install, modify, or keep a score
      enabled lies with you.</strong>
    </p>

    <h2>Network ingestion</h2>
    <p>
      Tempo's ingestion server accepts events from other hosts on your local
      network, protected by per-provider authentication tokens. You are
      responsible for the security of your local network, for the sources you
      authorize to send events, and for the secrets you configure. Tempo's
      role is to receive and display what you've authorized; it cannot audit
      the intent of the senders on your behalf.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party software</h2>
    <p>
      Tempo uses and bundles third-party open source components, notably:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Sparkle</strong> (MIT-licensed, <a href="https://sparkle-project.org">sparkle-project.org</a>): auto-update framework</li>
      <li><strong>GRDB.swift</strong> (MIT-licensed, <a href="https://github.com/groue/GRDB.swift">github.com/groue/GRDB.swift</a>): SQLite wrapper</li>
      <li><strong>SQLite</strong> (public domain, <a href="https://sqlite.org">sqlite.org</a>): embedded database</li>
      <li>Apple frameworks (SwiftUI, AppKit, Foundation, EventKit): used under the macOS SDK license</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Each component is used under its respective license, preserved within
      the application bundle and reachable in this document. A consolidated
      <em>About → Acknowledgements</em> panel inside the app is planned for a
      future release.
    </p>

    <h2>Trademarks</h2>
    <p>
      "Tempo" and the tempoapp.app domain are claimed by the project author.
      You may refer to Tempo by name in blog posts, reviews, screenshots, and
      other commentary. Do not use the name or visual identity to imply
      endorsement of unrelated products or services.
    </p>

    <h2>Freeware status and future changes</h2>
    <p>
      Tempo v1.x is and will remain <strong>freeware</strong>. Future major
      versions (v2 and beyond) may introduce a paid tier; existing installs of
      v1.x will remain fully usable at no cost.
    </p>
    <p>
      After v2 ships, v1.x will continue to receive <strong>security fixes
      only</strong>: no new features, no behavioural changes, no upgrades
      to existing functionality. Support for v1.x will move to
      <strong>community channels</strong> (Discord, GitHub Discussions);
      direct support from the publisher will be focused primarily on v2 and
      later releases.
    </p>
    <p>
      Any change to licensing or pricing will be announced on
      <a href="/">tempoapp.app</a> and in the application's release notes,
      with adequate notice.
    </p>

    <h2>Termination</h2>
    <p>
      The license granted above remains in effect for as long as you comply
      with these terms. If you materially breach the restrictions (for
      example, by redistributing or reselling the application binary without
      authorisation, or by reverse-engineering it outside of the limits
      permitted by applicable law), the license terminates automatically and
      you must cease using and distributing the affected copies. Termination
      does not waive any other remedy available under law.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may stop using Tempo at any time by quitting the application and
      removing it from your Mac. There is nothing to cancel and no account to
      close on our side.
    </p>

    <h2>Jurisdiction</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of Italy, without regard to
      conflict-of-law principles. If any provision is found unenforceable in
      your jurisdiction, the remaining provisions continue to apply.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you are a consumer resident in the European Union, the United Kingdom,
      or any other jurisdiction whose laws grant you mandatory consumer rights
      that cannot be waived by contract, those rights remain in force and are
      not affected by the choice of Italian law above. You may bring a claim
      in the competent court of the country where you reside.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="mailto:hello@tempoapp.app">hello@tempoapp.app</a>
    </p>
  </main>

  <style>
    .legal {
      max-width: 720px;
      margin: 48px auto;
      padding: 0 24px 80px;
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      line-height: 1.65;
      color: var(--text);
    }
    .legal .back {
      font-size: 14px;
      margin-bottom: 32px;
    }
    .legal .back a {
      color: var(--blue);
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    .legal h1 {
      font-size: 32px;
      margin-bottom: 8px;
      color: var(--text);
    }
    .legal h2 {
      font-size: 20px;
      margin-top: 40px;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
      color: var(--text);
    }
    .legal .meta {
      font-size: 13px;
      color: var(--text2);
      margin-bottom: 32px;
    }
    .legal .lede {
      font-size: 17px;
      color: var(--text);
      padding: 16px 20px;
      background: var(--bg2);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 8px;
      margin-bottom: 32px;
    }
    .legal ul { padding-left: 22px; }
    .legal li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
    .legal code {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.9em;
      background: var(--bg2);
      padding: 2px 6px;
      border-radius: 4px;
      color: var(--text);
    }
    .legal a { color: var(--blue); }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
